3. MEMORY SYSTEM SPECIFICATION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

3.1 ARCHITECTURE: LRU-Based Multi-Tier Storage
───────────────────────────────────────────────

STRUCTURE:
  • OrderedDict for O(1) LRU operations
  • Token-based inverted index for fast search
  • 3-tier aging system (HOT/WARM/COLD)
  • Encrypted persistence to disk

MEMORY ENTRY SCHEMA:
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ id:              string (timestamp + hash)                                  │
│ content:         {                                                          │
│   text:            string (pattern text)                                    │
│   embedding:       float[768] (semantic vector)                             │
│   tokens:          string[] (first 20 words)                                │
│   prompt:          string (what generated this)                             │
│ }                                                                           │
│ score:           float (alignment score, 0.0-1.0)                           │
│ friction:        float (constraint cost, 0.0-1.0)                           │
│ created:         timestamp                                                  │
│ last_accessed:   timestamp                                                  │
│ access_count:    integer                                                    │
│ tier:            enum {HOT, WARM, COLD}                                     │
│ amplification:   float (persistence factor)                                 │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

3.2 STORAGE TIERS
─────────────────

HOT Tier (0-30 days):
  • Recently created or frequently accessed
  • Always cached in memory
  • Used for active generation
  • Target: 1000-2000 patterns

WARM Tier (30-90 days):
  • Moderate age, occasional access
  • May be cached or on-disk
  • Retrieved when relevant
  • Target: 5000-10000 patterns

COLD Tier (90-365 days):
  • Old, rarely accessed
  • Primarily on-disk
  • Candidate for pruning
  • Target: Unlimited until pruned

PRUNING RULES:
  • Age > 365 days AND access_count < 3 → DELETE
  • Total memories > max_memories → prune oldest COLD
  • Friction > 0.85 for 30 days → fade (reduce amplification)

3.3 SEARCH ALGORITHM
────────────────────

INPUT: query_tokens (string[]), gel_state (1-10), k (results)

PROCESS:
  1. Extract query tokens (first 20 words)
  2. Lookup in token index → candidate_ids (set intersection)
  3. Filter by gel state accessibility
  4. Score each candidate:
       score = memory.score * (1 - memory.friction) * tier_bonus * recency

       tier_bonus = {HOT: 1.5, WARM: 1.0, COLD: 0.5}
       recency = 1.0 / (1.0 + age_hours / 24.0)

  5. Sort by score descending
  6. Return top-k
  7. Update access_count and last_accessed for retrieved memories

OUTPUT: List[(memory_id, score, content)]

3.4 STORAGE REQUIREMENTS
────────────────────────

PER MEMORY:
  • Text: ~200 bytes (avg)
  • Embedding: 768 * 4 = 3KB
  • Metadata: ~100 bytes
  • Total: ~3.3KB per memory

AT SCALE:
  • 10K memories: ~33MB
  • 100K memories: ~330MB
  • 1M memories: ~3.3GB

DISK FORMAT:
  • Encrypted JSONL (Fernet cipher)
  • Token index separate (pickle or sqlite)
  • Lazy load COLD tier on demand


