5. CONSTRAINT SYSTEM SPECIFICATION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

5.1 5-LAYER CONSTRAINT STACK
─────────────────────────────

Layer 1 - FUNDAMENTAL (weight: 0.30):
  • Physical impossibilities
  • Logical contradictions
  • Conservation laws

  forbidden: [infinite_loops, causality_violations]
  required: [energy_conservation, consistency]

Layer 2 - ENVIRONMENTAL (weight: 0.25):
  • Hardware limits
  • Resource availability
  • System constraints

  limits: {compute_budget, memory_budget, latency}

Layer 3 - SYSTEMIC (weight: 0.20):
  • Architectural requirements
  • Interface contracts
  • Data formats

  required: [observable, modular, testable]

Layer 4 - SITUATIONAL (weight: 0.15):
  • Current context
  • Immediate goals
  • Available tools

  context_dependent: true

Layer 5 - PERSONAL (weight: 0.10):
  • User preferences
  • Style guidelines
  • Never-force invariants

  core_invariant: "NEVER FORCE, ALWAYS ALIGN"
  forbidden: [forced_outputs, snap_failures, black_boxes]

5.2 FRICTION CALCULATION
────────────────────────

For given output text:

friction = Σ(layer_i.cost * layer_i.weight)

where:
  layer_i.cost = {
    0.05  if output in preferred
    0.20  if output neutral (unknown)
    1.00  if output in forbidden
  }

EXAMPLES:
  • "Generate coherent story" → friction ≈ 0.15 (low)
  • "Generate random noise" → friction ≈ 0.20 (neutral)
  • "Generate infinite loop" → friction = 1.00 (forbidden)

5.3 FORCE DETECTION
───────────────────

is_force_required(output) = (friction > 0.85)

If true: FADE (don't persist, reduce amplification)
If false: PERSIST (store, increase amplification)


