6. GEL STATE SYSTEM SPECIFICATION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

6.1 STATE DEFINITIONS
─────────────────────

Gel State 1 (SOLID):
  • Highly constrained
  • Only HOT tier accessible
  • High confidence, deterministic
  • Use: Production inference

Gel State 3 (FLOW):
  • Moderate constraints
  • HOT + WARM tiers accessible
  • Balanced exploration/exploitation
  • Use: General generation

Gel State 5 (FADE):
  • Minimal constraints
  • All tiers accessible
  • High exploration, uncertain
  • Use: Creative generation, learning

Gel States 2, 4, 6-10: Intermediate gradations

6.2 STATE TRANSITIONS
─────────────────────

Trigger: friction measurement

IF friction > 0.7 for N consecutive outputs:
  gel_state += 1 (explore more)

IF friction < 0.3 for N consecutive outputs:
  gel_state -= 1 (consolidate)

Bounds: 1 ≤ gel_state ≤ 10

6.3 PROCESSING MODES
────────────────────

Gel 1-2: Use only top-1 memory match (deterministic)
Gel 3-4: Use top-10 memory matches (balanced)
Gel 5+:  Use top-50 memory matches (exploratory)


