7. REALITY TETHER SPECIFICATION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

7.1 OBSERVATION SOURCES
───────────────────────

PRIMARY: System BIO (CPU/Memory load)
  • CPU usage: 0-100%
  • Memory usage: 0-100%
  • Energy = 1.0 - (cpu + mem) / 2.0
  • Rationale: High load = less energy available = higher friction

SECONDARY: OS Entropy
  • /dev/urandom
  • Pure randomness fallback

TERTIARY: Synthetic
  • Time-based pulse
  • Last resort

7.2 ENERGY CALCULATION
──────────────────────

energy = 1.0 - system_load

where:
  system_load = (cpu_percent + memory_percent) / 200.0

Effect: System busy → low energy → penalize expensive operations

7.3 ALIGNMENT SCORE
───────────────────

alignment = (1 - friction) * energy * relevance

where:
  friction:  constraint cost (0-1)
  energy:    system capacity (0-1)
  relevance: memory match score (0-1)

Decision:
  IF alignment > 0.6: PERSIST pattern
  ELSE: FADE pattern


