8. PATTERN TRACKER SPECIFICATION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

8.1 PATTERN LIFECYCLE
─────────────────────

NEW PATTERN:
  → record(content, friction)
  → amplification = 1.0
  → store in memory

PATTERN REUSE:
  → access_count++
  → amplification *= 1.2 (if friction < 0.3)
  → amplification *= 0.8 (if friction > 0.7)
  → cap: 0.1 ≤ amplification ≤ 3.0

PATTERN FADE:
  → amplification < 0.2 for 30 days → mark for deletion
  → OR age > 365 days AND access_count < 3 → prune

8.2 AMPLIFICATION DYNAMICS
──────────────────────────

Low-friction patterns AMPLIFY:
  • Easier to retrieve
  • Higher boost in generation
  • More likely to persist

High-friction patterns FADE:
  • Lower retrieval score
  • Reduced boost
  • Eventually pruned

Result: System naturally reinforces aligned patterns, fades misaligned ones.


