9. IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

9.1 PERFORMANCE TARGETS
───────────────────────

Memory Search:
  • <10ms for 10K memories
  • <100ms for 100K memories
  • <1s for 1M memories

Generation:
  • 10-50 tokens/second (CPU)
  • 100-500 tokens/second (GPU)

Memory Storage:
  • <1ms per pattern store
  • <100ms for full persistence to disk

9.2 LANGUAGE REQUIREMENTS
─────────────────────────

Core System: Rust or C++
  • Memory management critical
  • Performance sensitive
  • Production-grade reliability

Bindings: Python (for research/prototyping)
  • PyO3 (Rust) or pybind11 (C++)
  • Maintain API compatibility

9.3 DEPENDENCIES
────────────────

REQUIRED:
  • Embedding model (sentence-transformers or equivalent)
  • Tokenizer (BPE or WordPiece)
  • Crypto library (for memory encryption)
  • JSON parser

OPTIONAL:
  • GPU support (CUDA/Metal)
  • HTTP server (for API deployment)
  • Database (for scaling beyond memory)

9.4 API SURFACE
───────────────

Core Functions:

  initialize(config: Config) -> System
  load_memory(path: string) -> Memory

  generate(prompt: string, max_tokens: int, gel_state: int) -> Response
  store_pattern(text: string, score: float) -> MemoryID
  search_memory(query: string, k: int) -> Memory[]

  get_stats() -> Stats
  save_checkpoint(path: string)
  load_checkpoint(path: string)

